# CIRCUIT_GENERATION_INFO

Provenance of every circuit in `circuits/`, reconstructed from the project memory
records (`~/.claude/projects/.../memory/`) and confirmed against each file's
on-disk gate count/format. Generated 2026-07-10.

Where a run is fully documented, exact parameters are given. Where the records do
not cover a file (mostly older June files), that is stated explicitly as
**UNRECORDED** rather than guessed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 0. File formats

- **g57** — base-83 `repr()` text, one line, `;`-separated 3-wire gates
  `[target, pos_ctrl, neg_ctrl]` computing `t ^= pos OR NOT neg`. Gate count =
  number of `;`. All ssg/sss mixer outputs and their checkpoints are g57.
- **mpmct1** — header `mpmct1 <wires> <gates>` then one gate/line
  `target comp k w p ...` (mixed-polarity multi-controlled Toffolis, `comp=1`
  marks a surviving original g57 = "fossil"). All `fsplit` / `fmix` / `fcompress`
  outputs are mpmct1. Read back with `--input-format mpmct1`.
- Feistelize+slice deliverables carry a 2-line `# y=0x…` / `# z=0x…` header
  before the g57 body.

## 1. Pipeline primitives (the building blocks referenced below)

- **genran** — `local_mixing_bin genran -n <wires> -m <gates>`: a fresh random
  reversible g57 circuit. Used as raw sources C, D, or standalone.
- **compose_A.py sandwich** — `A = [C on wires 0..n-1] ++ n CNOT-blocks (6 g57
  each, w_{n+i} ^= w_i) ++ [D on wires 0..n-1]`. For n=128, m=3000: **A = 6768
  g57 gates / 256 wires**, self-testing A ≡ F(x,y) = (D(C(x)), y⊕C(x)). This is
  the "cdcnot" block-cipher construction.
- **gadgetize** — `ssg -n 256 -m 0 -x 10 --gadgetize`: expands the 256-wire A to
  a ~67k-gate / **512-wire** g57 circuit (stage 0 of the sm/es/r/sl/cmp runs).
- **ssg** — the generation-mixing mixer (variant of sss). Shoots/compresses in
  size-thermostatted stages; every gate carries a generation tag; `--min-gen G`
  stops when a fraction of gates reach generation ≥ G. Output is all-g57.
- **fsplit** — post-mixer (`src/postprocessing/`, this project). Floats a g57 to a
  collision and splits it past via the R0–R3 commutation rules, growing the
  circuit toward `--size-bound`. Knobs: `--k-max K` (max controls/gate),
  `--split-damp D` ("c"; a c-control gate splits w.p. min(2^-(c-D),1)),
  `--seed`, and (later builds) g57×g57 collision targeting (`--g57-target-window`,
  the "g57t" suffix). Surviving g57s = fossils; output mpmct1.
- **fmix** — randomized size-thermostatted mixing chain over the mpmct1 gate set
  (R-crossings + fresh-wire splits + merges under a temperature thermostat), a
  *replacement* for fsplit whose goal is mixing at a held size. Knobs:
  `--target-size`, `--moves`, `--k-max`, `--split-damp` (c), `--seed`.
  `fmixdirect` = fmix run directly on an ssg g57 output (no fsplit stage);
  `_fmix_` (plain) = fmix on an fsplit artifact; `fmixgad` = fmix on a gadgetized
  A with no ssg at all. `.snapshot.mv<N>` = verified mid-run snapshot at N moves.
- **fcompress** (`.fc`) — deterministic ESOP/ANF final compression pass
  (attacker-computable "effective size"); gathers same-target gates, ANF-reduces,
  re-emits mpmct1. Optional dead-cone pruning via `--live-wires`.
- **feistelize + slice_zero_random** — `--feistalize --slice-zero-random`: turns a
  genran source into a 384-wire feistelized circuit with a public (y,z) slice.

