## prodshare_n128_33_x3_final.mpmct1 (2026-07-25, from the server ~/tds/prod33_20260726)
Third production circuit through the PRODUCT-SHARE nonlinear encoding, and the
first under the BAND-HARDENING revision (commit 6aa54212; see
docs/BAND_HARDENING.{tex,pdf} and docs/NONLINEAR_GADGETIZATION.{tex,pdf}).
Four changes vs the [2,3,3] circuit above: the [3,3] plan (two deg-3 tower
terms, NO deg-2 base term -- 22% fewer gates; two terms is the measured floor,
a single term revives the deg-1 diagonal at rho 0.995), the band is now part
of the INPUT SLICE (a nonzero band used to change nothing, which separated
band from aux in two queries), a ROLLING BAND (the band variable's wire moves
via RG2's swap, erasing a census that named the band exactly: writes/wire
10-22 vs the carriers' 209-1004 before, indistinguishable after), and the
wide fold path now shuffles its fragments (that fix had only ever reached the
narrow path).
Pipeline:
  fresh C (128w x 3000 g57, SECRET, server-side only; gen_sandwich_gadget
  seed 71 -- note the args are POSITIONAL: <out> n m_C m_D s rg_freq
  slice_gates seed gadget_seed sandwich_seed, so s=896 rg_freq=1
  slice_gates=2560 must be passed explicitly to reach the seeds) ->
  sliced_sandwich_cnot (m_C=m_D=3000, s=896) = 7920 g / 256w ->
  product-share gadgetize (PROD_K=0 PROD_K_HI=2 PROD_DEG_HI=3 PROD_FILL_NL=2
  PROD_ROLL=1 => plan [3,3], band 46): 246808 g / 558 w, endpoint verify
  PASSED (low-256 == sandwich, 200 samples) ->
  fmix (FROZEN_DB_DIR=frozen_m1_m11, guards deg9/span30/terms 1024:2048):
  - PHASE A (generation-100 dose over the DB-TARGETABLE material, seed 71):
    --w-db 1.0 --gen-target 100 --gen-bias 0.9 --gen-giveup 30
    --gen-stop-frac 0.02 --p-db-ingest 0.25 --p-db-hard 0.05 --db-ctrl-cap 2
    --no-local-verify --p-twist 0.0016 neg-only, target 246808,
    --moves 12000000 as a CEILING -> DOSE REACHED AT 8.2M MOVES, 474950 g.
    NOTE: this is the first run where the dose stop could fire. Since
    512ce31c, G= is the 5th-percentile generation over the TARGETABLE gates
    (cap-eligible minus written-off) and dose_reached() tests lag/targetable;
    both were measured over ALL gates before, which on ~60%-wide material
    floors near 0.38 and can never trigger. G= climbed 0 -> 71 -> 82 -> 100
    while the legacy Gall= stayed pinned at 0 throughout; 52 gates written
    off. The fix only bites with --db-ctrl-cap > 0 (with the default 0 every
    gate counts as targetable and the statistic silently reverts).
    Size still drifts (+92%): the ingest/paid rounds are taken before the
    thermostat, so --target-size does not hold it -- but the run now stops
    when the dose is delivered rather than when the budget runs out.
    g57-shaped gates 42934 -> 329685 (the DB emits g57-shaped material).
    Wall clock 2043 s. Script run.sh (phases A and B; phase B there uses the
    superseded target -- see the note below).
  - PHASE B (grow to 3x PHASE B'S OWN INPUT = 3 x 474950 = 1424850): k-max 12
    --split-base 2.0 --no-local-verify --p-twist 0.001 neg-only, 15M moves
    (there is no size-based stop; the walk reaches target around move 1.7M and
    churns there for the rest of the budget) -> 1428155 g, x3.01 of its input.
    g57-shaped gates 329685 -> 637 (0.04% of the circuit -- better than the
    previous delivery's 1758, since erosion is crossing-driven and this run
    does more growth). Wall clock 3452 s. Script phaseB2.sh.
    NOTE ON THE TARGET: "triple the size" means 3x the size phase B STARTS
